# Hardware (one thread, the top of the physical-hardware subtree)
# hardware/__init__.py - owns Arduino, U2D2, every Male/Female/Bar, AllNeopixels, Bodies. Not started by main.py directly - only started via Exposition.setup() (see thread-exposition.timeline), or by manually clicking "start" on /app/hardware in the web UI. Until one of those happens, none of the autonomous behavior below runs at all. Every body is expanded inline below, in the exact order setup() starts them (Bodies.__iter__ yields males then females, then the bar is started last).

0 setup(): starts every Male and every Female (iterating Bodies, started_by=self), then starts the Bar (started_by=self) - all six start together on this same tick, expanded below in iteration order
-> thread-male : male1
-> thread-male : male2
-> thread-female : female1
-> thread-female : female2
-> thread-female : female3
-> thread-bar
0 loop(): pass - Hardware itself does no per-tick work; everything above runs independently once started
0 repeats every ~10ms tick, doing nothing - all real activity happens in the male/female/bar threads and everything they in turn start
0 setdown(): stops every Male and Female (iterating Bodies); doesn't explicitly stop the Bar - the Bar is still stopped via the children-stop mechanism (it was started with started_by=self), same pattern noted in thread-female.timeline and thread-bar.timeline
